"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2796,"Narrated to us Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Ishaq al-Azraq, narrated to us Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik (RA), saying, ""Inform me of something you have retained from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."" I said, ""Where did he pray Zuhr on the Day of Tarwiyah?"" He (RA) said, ""At Mina."" I said, ""Where did he pray Asr on the Day of Nafr?"" He (RA) said, ""At al-Abtaḥ."" Then he (RA) said, ""Do as your leaders have done.""

**CHAPTER:**"
2797,"**
Narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, Ahmad ibn Mani', and Muhammad ibn Hisham — they said: Narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash, who narrated: Narrated to us 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', who said: I met Anas ibn Malik (RA) on a donkey, heading towards Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah. So I asked him: ""Where did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pray Zuhr today?"" He said: ""He prayed where your leaders pray.""

Ibn Hisham added from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay': [This narration is also reported with this wording.]"
